        "how_it_works": "MACD compares a fast and a slow EMA; its signal line smooths that difference. A cross of the MACD line above the signal line (histogram turning positive) suggests momentum is picking up. Requiring the close to be above EMA 50 (or below it, for sells) keeps trades on the side of the broader move.",
        "struggles": "Choppy markets give frequent, small crosses that reverse quickly. Like every moving-average tool it reacts after the move has started, so entries can be late and exits give back profit.",
